<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_BlueIce.xml                             BLUEDESERT_RULED_CONTENT_1 §3

  The item form of the mineable (ThingDefs_Buildings/RM_BlueIceMineable.xml).
  NOT a hydrocarbon product — unlike RM_ColdWax this is real distilled-purity
  water-ice, the top row of the water taxonomy
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/water_taxonomy.csv, id blue_ice, added this
  change). It carries none of ColdWax's warm-detonation comps: water does not
  explode when it warms, it melts.

  Stockpilable/tradeable per the item's own scope line. MarketValue set here
  (unlike ColdWax, which parks pricing on ECONOMY_TRADE_SWEEP_1) because the
  sheet gives an explicit qualitative anchor — owner: "golden," i.e.
  distinctly valuable premium water, not merely another stone — so a
  plausible non-zero number belongs on the def rather than defaulting to 0
  and reading as worthless. FOUNDRY tunes in playtest per the bible's own
  "numbers are design choices" note.

  🔴 STUB HOOKUP POINT for BLUEDESERT_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 §7 (the Cold Hold):
  "blue-ice blocks as the ship's water stock" — this item is the row that
  ship-contribution wires to; nothing here needs to change for that, the
  item just needs to exist, which it now does.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_BlueIce</defName>
    <label>blue ice</label>
    <description>A cut block of the oldest ice on the plateau, quarried clean: deep glacial blue shot through with fine white crack-veils, clear enough at the thinnest edge to see a hand through. Distilled-grade water, frozen -- and worth quarrying for exactly that, in a desert with no water anywhere else.</description>
    <possessionCount>10</possessionCount>
    <tickerType>Never</tickerType>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_BlueIce/RM_BlueIce</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.9</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>3</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0</DeteriorationRate>
      <MarketValue>8</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
